Subject: [PATCH 159/160] tune: the CineCam Grade panel now follows the size of
 its dock

The wheels were a fixed 128 px in a left-packed row, so a wide dock left a
gap and a narrow one clipped them.

- the disc takes the width its control is given (72-208 px, quantised to 8)
  and drives its own height to match, so it stays circular and all three
  stay equal; only its maximum moves, so the panel can still shrink
- one breakpoint at 520 px: three wheels in a row above it, stacked below
- the wheel columns and the four numeric fields carry the stretch instead
  of a trailing spacer
- the wheel image is only rebuilt when the diameter actually changes, not
  on every resize frame of a dock drag

Layout only: binding, undo and the write path are untouched.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ADgAiBYv9AxSd54s1FPREm
